Fiber Network Designer at Ohio Gig | LinkedIn

Ohio Gig
Fiber Network Designer
Columbus, Ohio, United States · 4 days ago · 1 applicant
$60K/yr - $75K/yr · Full-time · Associate

Skills: Graphic Design · Photoshop · Network Architecture · Network Design · Internet Protocol (IP)

About the job
Ohio Gig is a dynamic and rapidly growing fiber internet service provider dedicated to bringing fast, reliable, and affordable internet connectivity to Ohio communities.

As a Fiber Network Designer, you will be responsible for designing our fiber optic networks from scratch, ensuring they meet or exceed customer and regulatory requirements.

Responsibilities:
Review and analyze data from CAD drawings, GIS (Geographic Information Systems) reports, and drone aerial photography.
Design fiber optic networks using industry-standard tools and best practices.
Create and update maps, drawings, and documentation for fiber optic network projects.
Collaborate with engineering, construction, and permitting teams to ensure designs meet project requirements.
Ensure compliance with local, state, and federal regulations.
Assist with make-ready engineering assessments.
Ensure proper documentation for each project.


Requirements:
BS degree or higher in Computer Science, Electrical Engineering, or related field (or equivalent experience).
Experience with fiber design tools such as AutoCAD, Katapult, GIS mapping software, or similar platforms is highly desirable but not required.
Ability to work with large data sets.
Ability to travel throughout Ohio as needed.
Strong problem-solving skills and attention to detail.

</tool_response>

